1
00:00:00,433 --> 00:00:02,467
Are you a SMART fella...

2
00:00:02,467 --> 00:00:04,533
or a FART smella?

3
00:00:04,533 --> 00:00:06,800
Let's find OUT!

4
00:00:07,733 --> 00:00:10,433
Question one! Which one does NOT

5
00:00:10,433 --> 00:00:13,467
belong? Robin... sparrow...

6
00:00:13,467 --> 00:00:16,333
salmon... eagle. Is it A,

7
00:00:16,333 --> 00:00:19,133
robin... B, sparrow...

8
00:00:19,267 --> 00:00:21,467
C, salmon... or D,

9
00:00:21,467 --> 00:00:24,167
eagle? Five seconds, go!

10
00:00:29,767 --> 00:00:32,300
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

11
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:34,200
The answer is...

12
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:37,000
C, salmon! A robin,

13
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:39,200
a sparrow, and an eagle all

14
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:41,333
soar through the sky as birds.

15
00:00:41,333 --> 00:00:42,367
But a salmon?

16
00:00:42,367 --> 00:00:43,800
That one swims.

17
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:45,367
It's a fish!

18
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:48,833
Question two, a number series!

19
00:00:48,833 --> 00:00:50,967
Three, six, twelve,

20
00:00:50,967 --> 00:00:53,000
twenty-four, and then...

21
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:54,367
what comes next?

22
00:00:54,367 --> 00:00:56,700
A, thirty-six... B,

23
00:00:56,700 --> 00:00:59,100
forty-eight... C, thirty...

24
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:01,000
or D, forty-two?

25
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,533
Five seconds!

26
00:01:08,100 --> 00:01:10,633
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

27
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:13,633
It's... B, forty-eight!

28
00:01:13,633 --> 00:01:15,633
Each number simply doubles:

29
00:01:15,633 --> 00:01:17,833
three, six, twelve,

30
00:01:17,833 --> 00:01:19,733
twenty-four... and twenty-four

31
00:01:19,733 --> 00:01:22,333
times two is forty-eight!

32
00:01:23,233 --> 00:01:25,933
Question three, a picture puzzle!

33
00:01:25,933 --> 00:01:28,433
An empty circle becomes a filled-in

34
00:01:28,433 --> 00:01:31,467
circle. So an empty square becomes...

35
00:01:31,467 --> 00:01:32,933
which one? A,

36
00:01:32,933 --> 00:01:34,333
a filled square...

37
00:01:34,333 --> 00:01:36,667
B, an empty square...

38
00:01:36,767 --> 00:01:38,533
C, a filled circle...

39
00:01:38,533 --> 00:01:40,967
or D, a filled triangle?

40
00:01:40,967 --> 00:01:42,433
Five seconds!

41
00:01:47,933 --> 00:01:50,467
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

42
00:01:50,833 --> 00:01:52,233
The answer is...

43
00:01:52,233 --> 00:01:54,467
A, a filled square!

44
00:01:54,467 --> 00:01:56,033
The rule is simple:

45
00:01:56,033 --> 00:01:57,633
the shape gets colored in,

46
00:01:57,633 --> 00:02:00,000
but stays the very same shape.

47
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:03,333
Empty square becomes filled square!

48
00:02:04,233 --> 00:02:06,967
Question four, a word analogy!

49
00:02:06,967 --> 00:02:08,733
Giant is to tiny,

50
00:02:08,733 --> 00:02:10,733
as wide is to...

51
00:02:10,733 --> 00:02:13,067
what? A, narrow...

52
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:15,167
B, tall... C,

53
00:02:15,167 --> 00:02:16,933
long... or D,

54
00:02:16,933 --> 00:02:19,800
big? Five seconds, go!

55
00:02:25,367 --> 00:02:27,900
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

56
00:02:28,300 --> 00:02:30,700
It's... A, narrow!

57
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:33,267
Giant and tiny are opposites,

58
00:02:33,267 --> 00:02:35,167
so just flip 'wide' to its

59
00:02:35,167 --> 00:02:37,900
opposite, and that's narrow!

60
00:02:38,867 --> 00:02:41,867
Question five, another number series!

61
00:02:41,867 --> 00:02:44,067
One hundred, ninety-two,

62
00:02:44,067 --> 00:02:47,533
eighty-four, seventy-six, and then...

63
00:02:47,533 --> 00:02:49,867
what? A, seventy...

64
00:02:49,867 --> 00:02:52,300
B, sixty-eight... C,

65
00:02:52,300 --> 00:02:54,500
sixty-six... or D,

66
00:02:54,500 --> 00:02:57,267
seventy-two? Five seconds!

67
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:05,333
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

68
00:03:05,633 --> 00:03:07,000
The answer is...

69
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:10,000
B, sixty-eight! Every step drops

70
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,333
by eight, and seventy-six minus

71
00:03:12,333 --> 00:03:14,200
eight is sixty-eight!

72
00:03:15,133 --> 00:03:17,867
Question six, a word analogy!

73
00:03:17,867 --> 00:03:19,267
Ocean is to puddle,

74
00:03:19,267 --> 00:03:21,167
as mountain is to...

75
00:03:21,167 --> 00:03:23,600
what? A, valley...

76
00:03:23,767 --> 00:03:26,000
B, hill... C,

77
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:27,633
river... or D,

78
00:03:27,633 --> 00:03:29,867
rock? Five seconds!

79
00:03:35,367 --> 00:03:37,900
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

80
00:03:38,267 --> 00:03:40,900
It's... B, hill!

81
00:03:40,900 --> 00:03:42,733
An ocean shrinks down to a

82
00:03:42,733 --> 00:03:45,067
tiny puddle, so a mountain shrinks

83
00:03:45,067 --> 00:03:46,800
down to a little hill.

84
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:49,300
Same thing, pocket-sized!

85
00:03:50,233 --> 00:03:52,733
Question seven, and this one is

86
00:03:52,733 --> 00:03:55,433
tricky! Two, six,

87
00:03:55,433 --> 00:03:58,267
twelve, twenty, thirty,

88
00:03:58,267 --> 00:04:01,233
and then... what comes next?

89
00:04:01,333 --> 00:04:04,000
A, thirty-six... B,

90
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:07,200
forty... C, forty-two...

91
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:09,567
or D, forty-four?

92
00:04:09,567 --> 00:04:11,400
Five seconds on the clock!

93
00:04:17,067 --> 00:04:19,600
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

94
00:04:19,967 --> 00:04:21,300
The answer is...

95
00:04:21,300 --> 00:04:24,267
C, forty-two! Look at the jumps:

96
00:04:24,267 --> 00:04:26,267
plus four, plus six,

97
00:04:26,267 --> 00:04:28,267
plus eight, plus ten.

98
00:04:28,267 --> 00:04:30,433
The next jump is plus twelve,

99
00:04:30,433 --> 00:04:33,567
and thirty plus twelve is forty-two!

100
00:04:34,567 --> 00:04:37,033
Question eight, a word analogy!

101
00:04:37,033 --> 00:04:38,700
Painter is to brush,

102
00:04:38,700 --> 00:04:40,833
as carpenter is to...

103
00:04:40,833 --> 00:04:42,967
what? A, hammer...

104
00:04:42,967 --> 00:04:45,400
B, wood... C,

105
00:04:45,400 --> 00:04:47,267
house... or D,

106
00:04:47,267 --> 00:04:49,267
nail? Five seconds!

107
00:04:54,767 --> 00:04:57,300
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

108
00:04:57,667 --> 00:04:59,500
It's... A, hammer!

109
00:04:59,500 --> 00:05:01,633
A painter's tool is a brush,

110
00:05:01,633 --> 00:05:03,367
and a carpenter's tool is a

111
00:05:03,367 --> 00:05:06,267
hammer. Wood is just the material,

112
00:05:06,267 --> 00:05:08,833
and a house is what you build!

113
00:05:09,733 --> 00:05:12,567
Question nine, a number series!

114
00:05:12,567 --> 00:05:14,600
One, one, two,

115
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:16,600
three, five, eight,

116
00:05:16,600 --> 00:05:19,067
and then... what comes next?

117
00:05:19,067 --> 00:05:21,067
A, eleven... B,

118
00:05:21,067 --> 00:05:23,600
thirteen... C, twelve...

119
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:25,733
or D, sixteen?

120
00:05:25,733 --> 00:05:27,167
Five seconds!

121
00:05:32,667 --> 00:05:35,200
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

122
00:05:35,533 --> 00:05:37,067
The answer is...

123
00:05:37,067 --> 00:05:39,733
B, thirteen! Add the two numbers

124
00:05:39,733 --> 00:05:41,933
before it: five plus eight is

125
00:05:41,933 --> 00:05:45,567
thirteen. That's the famous Fibonacci pattern!

126
00:05:46,533 --> 00:05:49,000
Question ten! Which one does NOT

127
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:52,000
belong? Add... subtract...

128
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,967
multiply... number. A,

129
00:05:54,967 --> 00:05:57,767
add... B, subtract...

130
00:05:58,033 --> 00:06:00,767
C, multiply... or D,

131
00:06:00,767 --> 00:06:03,400
number? Five seconds!

132
00:06:09,067 --> 00:06:11,600
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

133
00:06:11,967 --> 00:06:14,500
It's... D, number!

134
00:06:14,500 --> 00:06:17,167
Add, subtract, and multiply are

135
00:06:17,167 --> 00:06:18,467
all things you do.

136
00:06:18,467 --> 00:06:19,433
But a number?

137
00:06:19,433 --> 00:06:21,733
That's the thing you do them to!

138
00:06:22,633 --> 00:06:25,333
Question eleven, a shape puzzle!

139
00:06:25,333 --> 00:06:26,500
Watch them grow,

140
00:06:26,500 --> 00:06:28,767
gaining one side each step:

141
00:06:28,767 --> 00:06:30,867
a triangle, then a square,

142
00:06:30,867 --> 00:06:32,267
then a pentagon.

143
00:06:32,267 --> 00:06:34,067
Which shape comes next?

144
00:06:34,067 --> 00:06:35,467
A, a circle...

145
00:06:35,467 --> 00:06:37,600
B, a hexagon...

146
00:06:37,667 --> 00:06:39,033
C, a square...

147
00:06:39,033 --> 00:06:41,233
or D, an octagon?

148
00:06:41,233 --> 00:06:42,800
Five seconds!

149
00:06:48,333 --> 00:06:50,867
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

150
00:06:51,200 --> 00:06:52,667
The answer is...

151
00:06:52,667 --> 00:06:55,667
B, hexagon! Count the sides:

152
00:06:55,667 --> 00:06:58,267
triangle three, square four,

153
00:06:58,267 --> 00:07:00,967
pentagon five... so next up is

154
00:07:00,967 --> 00:07:03,500
the six-sided hexagon!

155
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:06,833
Question twelve, fill in the blank!

156
00:07:06,833 --> 00:07:08,500
The bridge was too weak to

157
00:07:08,500 --> 00:07:09,733
hold the heavy truck,

158
00:07:09,733 --> 00:07:11,633
so workers had to blank it

159
00:07:11,633 --> 00:07:13,200
before opening the road.

160
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:15,433
A, decorate... B,

161
00:07:15,433 --> 00:07:18,200
reinforce... C, rename...

162
00:07:18,200 --> 00:07:19,833
or D, measure?

163
00:07:19,833 --> 00:07:21,167
Five seconds!

164
00:07:26,667 --> 00:07:29,200
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

165
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:32,367
It's... B, reinforce!

166
00:07:32,367 --> 00:07:33,967
Too weak means you have to

167
00:07:33,967 --> 00:07:35,100
make it stronger,

168
00:07:35,100 --> 00:07:37,400
and reinforce is the only word

169
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:39,200
that fixes the problem!

170
00:07:40,067 --> 00:07:43,067
Question thirteen, a picture puzzle!

171
00:07:43,067 --> 00:07:45,333
A dot marches clockwise around

172
00:07:45,333 --> 00:07:47,200
a square: top-left,

173
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:49,433
top-right, bottom-right... where

174
00:07:49,433 --> 00:07:51,100
does it jump next?

175
00:07:51,200 --> 00:07:53,533
A, top-left... B,

176
00:07:53,533 --> 00:07:56,467
bottom-left... C, top-right...

177
00:07:56,467 --> 00:07:58,300
or D, the center?

178
00:07:58,300 --> 00:08:00,067
Five seconds!

179
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:08,133
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

180
00:08:08,433 --> 00:08:09,800
The answer is...

181
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:13,333
B, bottom-left! The dot steps clockwise,

182
00:08:13,333 --> 00:08:14,400
corner to corner,

183
00:08:14,400 --> 00:08:16,067
and right after bottom-right,

184
00:08:16,067 --> 00:08:18,467
the next corner is bottom-left!

185
00:08:19,333 --> 00:08:22,300
Question fourteen, a number analogy!

186
00:08:22,300 --> 00:08:23,433
Two makes five,

187
00:08:23,433 --> 00:08:24,633
three makes seven,

188
00:08:24,633 --> 00:08:25,900
four makes nine,

189
00:08:25,900 --> 00:08:27,433
so five makes...

190
00:08:27,433 --> 00:08:29,267
what? A, ten...

191
00:08:29,267 --> 00:08:31,233
B, eleven... C,

192
00:08:31,233 --> 00:08:32,867
twelve... or D,

193
00:08:32,867 --> 00:08:35,233
thirteen? Five seconds!

194
00:08:40,733 --> 00:08:43,267
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

195
00:08:43,667 --> 00:08:46,100
It's... B, eleven!

196
00:08:46,100 --> 00:08:47,567
Each number is doubled,

197
00:08:47,567 --> 00:08:49,000
then add one.

198
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:51,000
Five times two is ten,

199
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:53,300
plus one is eleven!

200
00:08:54,400 --> 00:08:56,867
Last one, question fifteen,

201
00:08:56,867 --> 00:08:58,300
a number puzzle,

202
00:08:58,300 --> 00:08:59,733
and it's sneaky!

203
00:08:59,733 --> 00:09:02,133
If four plus five makes twenty,

204
00:09:02,133 --> 00:09:04,433
three plus six makes eighteen,

205
00:09:04,433 --> 00:09:07,233
and two plus seven makes fourteen...

206
00:09:07,233 --> 00:09:10,033
then five plus four makes...

207
00:09:10,033 --> 00:09:12,433
what? A, nine...

208
00:09:12,467 --> 00:09:14,767
B, eighteen... C,

209
00:09:14,767 --> 00:09:16,367
twenty... or D,

210
00:09:16,367 --> 00:09:18,800
twenty-five? Five seconds!

211
00:09:24,267 --> 00:09:26,800
TIME'S UP! Pencils down!

212
00:09:27,100 --> 00:09:28,567
The answer is...

213
00:09:28,567 --> 00:09:31,000
C, twenty! Here's the trick:

214
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:34,300
that plus sign secretly means multiply.

215
00:09:34,300 --> 00:09:36,100
Four times five is twenty,

216
00:09:36,100 --> 00:09:39,200
so five times four is twenty too!

217
00:09:40,233 --> 00:09:43,167
So, are you smart or fart?

218
00:09:43,167 --> 00:09:44,933
Count up your correct answers to

219
00:09:44,933 --> 00:09:46,567
find your rank!

220
00:09:47,433 --> 00:09:49,033
So, how did you do?

221
00:09:49,033 --> 00:09:50,533
Comment your score below,

222
00:09:50,533 --> 00:09:52,367
and subscribe for more!
